 "note": "\"next arrival\" (this is the one reading that had to be chosen).**  The base head's\nown `stand_next_arr_inblock_dt` (`exp-018-fresh/code/features.py:264`) queries at the\nDEPARTURE'S TAKE-OFF, so it is never negative, and against it the constraint is VACUOUS: a\nviolation would need the off-block after an in-block that is itself at or after the\ntake-off, which is a negative taxi.  The reading used here is the next OCCUPANT: `P` is the\nlast same-stand arrival in-block at or before the take-off (in a turnaround, the row's own\ninbound) and `Q` is the first one strictly after `P`.  `Q` may fall before the take-off,\nand that is exactly the case with content -- the stand is re-occupied inside the row's own\ntaxi, so the true taxi is bounded BELOW by `take-off - Q`.  Both are label-free.  The\nreading rejected: querying at the take-off, which is the vacuous one, and it is reported\nbeside the answer so the desk can see the difference rather than take it on trust.",
